  "description": "The 2026 New Hampshire gubernatorial election will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect the governor of New Hampshire for a two-year term. Incumbent Republican Governor Kelly Ayotte is seeking a second term after winning the open seat in 2024 with 53.6% of the vote. The Democratic primary field has consolidated around former Executive Councilor Cinde Warmington, who lost the 2024 Democratic primary but is now the lone Democratic candidate following withdrawals by other potential contenders. New Hampshire is a politically competitive state that voted Democratic in the 2024 presidential election but has elected Republican governors in recent cycles, and the race is rated Lean Republican or Likely Republican by major election forecasters.",
